        "node_id": "n_15_a4cd25",
        "thought_text": "Iterate through all possible substrings $s[l..r]$ and simulate the reversal. Compare the resulting string with the original using lexicographical comparison. The first pair $(l, r)$ that yields a smaller string is a valid answer. While computationally expensive ($O(n^3)$ or $O(n^2)$ depending on implementation), it is a brute-force approach that guarantees correctness if a solution exists.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "8412054547025486182",
